   "source": [
    "# WaveNet Character-Level Language Model - Interactive Exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides an interactive exploration of the WaveNet character-level language model for name generation. You'll learn about the data, train the model, and generate new names!\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📚 What you'll learn:\n",
    "- Character-level language modeling fundamentals\n",
    "- WaveNet-inspired architecture\n",
    "- Training neural networks from scratch\n",
    "- Text generation techniques\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's get started! 🚀"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import required libraries\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add src to path for our custom modules\n",
    "sys.path.append('../src')\n",
    "\n",
    "from data_utils import prepare_data, print_sample_data\n",
    "from model import WaveNetCharModel, Trainer, Evaluator, NameGenerator, create_model_from_data\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set up plotting\n",
    "plt.style.use('default')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (10, 6)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ All imports successful!\")\n",
    "print(f\"🔥 PyTorch version: {torch.__version__}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📊 Step 1: Explore the Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's start by loading and exploring our names dataset. We'll see what the raw data looks like and how we convert it into training examples."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load the names data\n",
    "data_path = '../data/names.txt'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check if file exists\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(data_path):\n",
    "    print(f\"❌ Data file not found: {data_path}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please make sure names.txt is in the data/ directory\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ Found data file: {data_path}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Read some sample names\n",
    "    with open(data_path, 'r') as f:\n",
    "        names = f.read().splitlines()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\n📈 Dataset Statistics:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Total names: {len(names):,}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Average name length: {np.mean([len(name) for name in names]):.1f} characters\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Shortest name: {min(names, key=len)} ({len(min(names, key=len))} chars)\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Longest name: {max(names, key=len)} ({len(max(names, key=len))} chars)\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\n🎲 Random sample of 15 names:\")\n",
    "    import random\n",
    "    sample_names = random.sample(names, 15)\n",
    "    for i, name in enumerate(sample_names, 1):\n",
    "        print(f\"{i:2d}. {name}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize name length distribution\n",
    "name_lengths = [len(name) for name in names]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n",
    "plt.hist(name_lengths, bins=20, alpha=0.7, color='skyblue', edgecolor='black')\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Name Lengths')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Name Length (characters)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Frequency')\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n",
    "# Character frequency\n",
    "all_chars = ''.join(names).lower()\n",
    "char_counts = {}\n",
    "for char in all_chars:\n",
    "    char_counts[char] = char_counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n",
    "\n",
    "chars = sorted(char_counts.keys())\n",
    "counts = [char_counts[char] for char in chars]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.bar(chars, counts, alpha=0.7, color='lightcoral')\n",
    "plt.title('Character Frequency Distribution')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Character')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Frequency')\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"📊 Most common characters: {sorted(char_counts.items(), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)[:5]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔄 Step 2: Data Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's prepare the data for training. We'll create character mappings and build context-target pairs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Prepare the data with our preprocessing pipeline\n",
    "print(\"🔄 Preparing data for training...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use block size of 3 (context window)\n",
    "data_dict = prepare_data(data_path, block_size=3, train_ratio=0.8, val_ratio=0.1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract information\n",
    "datasets = data_dict['datasets']\n",
    "mappings = data_dict['mappings']\n",
    "config = data_dict['config']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✅ Data preparation complete!\")\n",
    "print(f\"📝 Vocabulary size: {mappings['vocab_size']} characters\")\n",
    "print(f\"🔤 Characters: {list(mappings['itos'].values())}\")\n",
    "print(f\"📊 Training examples: {config['train_size']:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"📊 Validation examples: {config['val_size']:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"📊 Test examples: {config['test_size']:,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get the training data\n",
    "X_train, Y_train = datasets['train']\n",
    "X_val, Y_val = datasets['val']\n",
